/Title (The rapid advancement of computer vision and deep learning has made facial analysis widely accessible, yet this capability remains fragmented across disconnected, purpose-built tools. Simultaneously, the proliferation of AI-generated synthetic media commonly known as deepfakes has introduced unprecedented threats to digital trust, identity verification, and personal safety. Traditional systems address only isolated aspects of these challenges, forcing practitioners and researchers to integrate multiple, incompatible tools with inconsistent accuracy and no unified interaction surface.)
